                     '15 years, and a bank or fund failure that takes deposits is rarer (estimate leaning on the big '
                     "falls in world share prices of recent generations); about half of such crashes cut a saver's "
                     'own savings hard enough to be a turning point, so about 3 in 100 savers a year in the working '
                     "and retired years, 2 in 100 young adults, who have less invested; 'a recession' (read) is the "
                     "slump in jobs and shops that often follows, and 'financial ruin' the bankruptcy that can come "
